1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:04,410
Add up only odd numbers
and you always get a square number?

2
00:00:04,460 --> 00:00:05,980
Start with 1 square

3
00:00:06,030 --> 00:00:08,500
Add the next odd number, 3, as an L shape

4
00:00:08,550 --> 00:00:11,980
A square! 2 × 2 = 4

5
00:00:12,030 --> 00:00:15,540
Add 5 and you get 3 × 3 = 9

6
00:00:15,590 --> 00:00:19,780
Each L shape = the next odd number

7
00:00:19,830 --> 00:00:22,750
Every new layer
makes the square one bigger

8
00:00:22,800 --> 00:00:27,660
So what if we add all the way to 19?

9
00:00:27,710 --> 00:00:31,160
Add 10 odd numbers and you get 100 = 10²

10
00:00:32,160 --> 00:00:35,910
NEXT: A square root (√) is squaring backwards!
